# Line endings are LF everywhere: in the repository, and in every working tree on every
# platform. Without this, a Windows clone with `core.autocrlf=true` gets CRLF files, and
# then rustfmt, gofmt, and CI disagree about what "formatted" means on a diff nobody
# changed. `eol=lf` settles it regardless of how a contributor's git is configured.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never rewrite their bytes, never diff them as text. Git's NUL-byte
# heuristic already classifies most of these correctly; naming them means no single
# unlucky file (161 `.dcp` camera profiles, for instance) can slip through as text.
*.dcp binary
*.dng binary
*.icns binary
*.ico binary
*.jpg binary
*.png binary
*.webp binary
*.woff2 binary
